    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25-a2">

                <pb facs="0161" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg37"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                    426.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Christitch to Mr.
                            Kasson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Principality of Servia,<lb/>Legation in
                                Austria-Hungary</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1881-02-13"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 13,
                    1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Ministre</hi>: I have just received the
                    response of the minister for foreign affairs following the communication of the
                    contents of the note which you were pleased to address to me on the 1st instant.
                    The government sincerely regrets that the present condition of our finances does
                    not allow it to nominate its representative near the United States of America;
                    still, it indulges the hope that the great and wealthy Republic will not for
                    that reason be less disposed to nominate its representative at Belgrade.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, Monsieur le Ministre, of this fresh occasion to renew to your
                    excellency the assurances of my highest consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>PH. CHRISTITCH.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">John A. Kasson</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary of
                            the United States of America, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., at
                        Vienna.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
